    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i guess you're right, it's probably just a technical thing. i'm just being dramatic because it's so cold lol. \n\nbut it is just so weird... like, i was sitting here and i actually heard this weird, tiny scratching or clicking sound coming from inside the wall right before it went dead. it wasn't a loud sound, just like... something small moving around. do you think that could be related to the pipes or a valve failing, or is that just my imagination playing tricks on me?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
